## Change review - 2026-10-28

**Static dependency recovery distinguishes assignments and Python package exports.** Reviewed commit `4e6d3299017a7432da15957874992837a315c5b4` (commit date `2026-10-26T15:05:22+08:00`). Compared with `1d7418b8abfa543744ae029e63a482aee03f9022`; the complete Git comparison contains 28 changed paths.

The Makefile target detector now rejects a line when an equals sign precedes its first colon, preventing substitution expressions and URL-valued assignments from becoming false build targets. Its new fixture covers OBJ substitution, a URL and exported PATH while retaining the build rule. The Python relative-import resolver adds package __init__.py fallback when an imported name is not a discovered submodule and handles star imports, while avoiding self edges and duplicate package edges. The fixture checks parent/current package exports, submodule precedence and self-import exclusion. This improves conservative static navigation; it does not execute Make, resolve arbitrary generated targets or prove that a Python exported name actually exists.

Evidence: [understand-anything-plugin/packages/core/src/plugins/parsers/makefile-parser.ts:20-55](https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything/blob/4e6d3299017a7432da15957874992837a315c5b4/understand-anything-plugin/packages/core/src/plugins/parsers/makefile-parser.ts#L20-L55) · [understand-anything-plugin/skills/understand/extract-import-map.mjs:970-1013](https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything/blob/4e6d3299017a7432da15957874992837a315c5b4/understand-anything-plugin/skills/understand/extract-import-map.mjs#L970-L1013) · [tests/skill/understand/test_extract_import_map.test.mjs:713-757](https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything/blob/4e6d3299017a7432da15957874992837a315c5b4/tests/skill/understand/test_extract_import_map.test.mjs#L713-L757) · [understand-anything-plugin/packages/core/src/__tests__/parsers.test.ts:520-539](https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything/blob/4e6d3299017a7432da15957874992837a315c5b4/understand-anything-plugin/packages/core/src/__tests__/parsers.test.ts#L520-L539).

**Harness consequence:** Retain parser/version provenance on code edges and distinguish syntactic candidate edges from runtime dependency certainty. Test false-positive and missed-edge patterns before using a code graph for impact analysis. Keep parser output advisory for task planning and confirm exact source spans before editing. Dashboard localization and plugin metadata in this refresh do not change those evidence limits.

**Scope and limits:** Scoped static review of both changed parser/resolver hunks and regression fixtures within the 28-path comparison. No source code or tests were executed. Dashboard translation, plugin installation, whole-language parsing coverage and dynamic import/Make evaluation were not audited.

